 collaborators at UPenn, Stanford, and the University of Washington. The icon comes from Ai2's official homepage. This represents the code-hosting research institution, not an exclusive affiliation for every author.","image","projectMedia","Creator project media","Source reviewed","2026-10-18","verified","Year","2023","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[85],"dimensions","Development stages",[155,156],"stages","Planning","Engines & scenes","Topics",[160,161,162,163],"tags","Text-to-scene","AI2-THOR","Spatial constraints","Embodied environments","Further reading",[166],{"_49":167,"_26":168},"Paper","https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.09067","Project source",[171],{"_49":169,"_26":172},"https://github.com/allenai/Holodeck","Why it belongs here","Combines language planning, asset retrieval, and spatial constraints to turn room requirements into AI2-THOR scenes, with instructions for loading them in Unity. Evaluation primarily targets embodied AI environment generation. It offers ideas for scene layout and semantic interaction, but does not establish complete game level design or commercial release readiness.","detail","Resource type","Framework","Category","3D development","category","summary","name","framework",[191],[160,161,162,163],[189,190],[102],2023,"plan","scene",{"_49":167,"_26":168},{"_193":194},"documents",{"_195":196,"_197":198},"en",[200,204,205,206,203,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223,224,225,226,227,228,229,230,231,232,233,234,235,236,237,238,202,239,201,240,241,242,243,244,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,252,253,254,255,256,257],"zh",[199,200,201,202,203],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies